From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:07:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: Program the ALC233 as the OEM firmware
 does

The verb table of the ALC233 (subsystem 17aa:3136) sets the same pin
configuration as the OEM firmware, and nothing else of the OEM table
for this codec and subsystem: the function reset, the Realtek
coefficients of the widgets 0x20 and 0x57, among them those the Linux
driver writes for the headset jack, and the speaker path (mixer gains,
pin 0x14 output and EAPD). The front audio jacks are listed as not
working on this board. Take the whole OEM table, in its order: 23 sets
of four verbs instead of 11.

TEST=The table, with the macros expanded, matches dword for dword the
one the OEM firmware of an M920x (machine type 10S2) holds for the
ALC233 and subsystem 17aa:3136, with the internal speaker. Built
lenovo/m920x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/hda_verb.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/hda_verb.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/hda_verb.c
index 6e6d679e26..8601470ae3 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/hda_verb.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/hda_verb.c
@@ -5,8 +5,9 @@
 const u32 cim_verb_data[] = {
 	0x10ec0235,	/* Codec Vendor / Device ID: Realtek ALC233 */
 	0x17aa3136,	/* Subsystem ID */
-	11,		/* Number of 4 dword sets */
+	23,		/* Number of 4 dword sets */
 	AZALIA_SUBVENDOR(0, 0x17aa3136),
+	AZALIA_RESET(1),
 	AZALIA_PIN_CFG(0, 0x12, 0x40000000),
 	AZALIA_PIN_CFG(0, 0x14, 0x90170110),
 	AZALIA_PIN_CFG(0, 0x17, AZALIA_PIN_CFG_NC(0)),
@@ -17,6 +18,19 @@ const u32 cim_verb_data[] = {
 	AZALIA_PIN_CFG(0, 0x1d, 0x40400001),
 	AZALIA_PIN_CFG(0, 0x1e, AZALIA_PIN_CFG_NC(0)),
 	AZALIA_PIN_CFG(0, 0x21, 0x0221101f),
+	/* Realtek coefficients (widgets 0x20 and 0x57), as the OEM firmware */
+	0x02050038, 0x02046991, 0x0205000d, 0x02042810,
+	0x05750003, 0x057486a6, 0x02050034, 0x02048204,
+	0x02050009, 0x0204e003, 0x0205004b, 0x02045555,
+	0x0205004a, 0x02043fc0, 0x0205003d, 0x020482ba,
+	0x02050039, 0x0204110f, 0x02050031, 0x0204e000,
+	0x02050037, 0x02044a05, 0x0205001b, 0x02040a0b,
+	0x02050046, 0x02040004, 0x02050010, 0x02040020,
+	0x02050040, 0x02041800, 0x02050008, 0x02046a0c,
+	0x05750003, 0x057486a6, 0x05750003, 0x057486a6,
+	/* The speaker: mixer gains, pin 0x14 output and EAPD, as the OEM firmware */
+	0x00b3f417, 0x00c3f11f, 0x00c3f001, 0x01470740,
+	0x01470740, 0x0143b000, 0x01470c02, 0x01470c02,
 
 	0x8086280b,	/* Codec Vendor / Device ID: Intel Kabylake HDMI */
 	0x80860101,	/* Subsystem ID */
-- 
